{"episodes":{"188761":"A broken line of thunderstorms ahead of a cold front moving across the eastern Gulf of Mexico produce gusty marine winds over the Nature Coast.","188799":"A slow moving cold front generated thunderstorms early in the morning of 3/27. One of these storms produced sub-severe hail.","188847":"Strong thunderstorms moved across Apalachee Bay with gusty winds of 34 knots measured at the St Marks Lighthouse.","188982":"Scattered thunderstorms moved across southern Lake Michigan during the late morning and early afternoon of March 26th.  High winds then developed during the afternoon and continued into the evening across southern Lake Michigan.","189148":"Steep mid-level lapse rates with sufficient instability ahead of a cold front sparked numerous thunderstorms across the area with severe weather.  Most of the reports were in the form of large hail, and wind damage was confined to the Valdosta area. However, significant wind damage did occur in Valdosta due to a downburst.","189155":"Steep mid-level lapse rates with sufficient instability ahead of a cold front sparked numerous thunderstorms across the area with severe weather.  Most of the reports were in the form of large hail, and wind damage was confined to the Valdosta area. However, significant wind damage did occur in Valdosta due to a downburst.","189306":"A couple waves of strong to severe storms moved across the region ahead of a cold front under passing short wave troughs.","189327":"An upper level trough pushed a warm front across South Central Texas and generated thunderstorms. One of these storms produced large hail.","189950":"Scattered showers and storms formed to our west/southwest during the afternoon of the 27th and moved east through North and Central Texas over the rest of the evening. One storm in Parker County produced quarter sized hail.","190042":"Weak afternoon convection was able to generate a landspout near Davenport."},"events":[{"begin":"2024-03-27T00:45Z","county":"Linco